      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "1. When rolling six 6-sided dice, the probability of getting four of the same number is $\\frac{1}{6}$.\n2. The probability of not getting four of the same number is $1 - \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{5}{6}$.\n\nTo determine the probability that when we roll four fair 6-sided dice, they collectively won't all show the same number, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the total number of possible outcomes when rolling four dice. Since each die has six faces, the total number of outcomes can be calculated as:\n   \\[\n   6^4 = 1296\n   \\]\n\n2. Let \\( A \\) denote the event that all four dice throw the same number.\n\n3. The event that \"all dice show the same number\" includes the following 6 scenarios:\n   \\[\n   A = \\{\\text{AAA}, \\text{BBB}, \\text{CCC}, \\text{DDD}, \\text{EEE}, \\text{FFF}\\}\n   \\]\n\n4. The probability of event \\( A \\), itself, occurs when all four dice roll the same face (face 1, face 2,..., or face 6):\n   \\[\n   \\mathbb{P}(A) = 6 \\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)^4 = 6 \\times \\frac{1}{6^4} = \\frac{1}{6}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the probability that the four dice won't all roll the same number is determined by:\n   \\[\n   \\mathbb{P}(A^c) = 1 - \\mathbb{P}(A)\n   \\]\nwhere \\( A^c \\) is the complement of \\( A \\), which is the event where all dice do not roll the same number.\n\n5. Substituting the calculated probability of event \\( A \\):\n   \\[\n   \\mathbb{P}(A^c) = 1 - \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{5}{6}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the four dice won't all roll the same number when rolled is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\frac{5}{6}}\n   \\]",
